From d5f37eb21df555e1603595c69dca283f373dfb3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:07:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] contacts: keep a writable account in sync with each sim
 card

sim contacts are only reachable through a one-shot import dialog and
edits never go back to the card. register a writable sim account per
subscription so sim entries appear in the contact list and new contacts
can target the sim, with name fields capped to the adn byte limit.

push local edits and deletions to the card before resyncing cp2, roll
back writes the sim rejects, store the record number right after
inserting so interrupted syncs do not duplicate entries, and follow sim
insertion and removal on carrier config changes.
